{
  "name": "Chef",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Ability Score Increase.</strong> Increase your Constitution or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p><p><strong>Cook’s Utensils.</strong> You gain proficiency with @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.equipment.Item.phbtulCooksUtens]{Cook’s Utensils} if you don’t already have it.</p><p><strong>Replenishing Meal.</strong> As part of a Short Rest, you can cook special food if you have ingredients and Cook’s Utensils on hand. You can prepare enough of this food for a number of creatures equal to 4 plus your Proficiency Bonus (currently [[4 + @prof]]). At the end of the Short Rest, any creature who eats the food and spends one or more Hit Dice to regain Hit Points regains an extra 1d8 Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Bolstering Treats.</strong> With 1 hour of work or when you finish a Long Rest, you can cook a number of treats equal to your Proficiency Bonus if you have ingredients and Cook’s Utensils on hand. These special treats last 8 hours after being made. A creature can use a Bonus Action to eat one of those treats to gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-onsn880Y02uWVh6N\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The <strong>Replenishing Meal</strong> activity includes the healing.</p><p>The <strong>Bolstering Treats</strong> activity will restore a number of uses equal to your Proficiency Bonus. As creatures eat them you can use the <strong>Eat Treat</strong> activity to reduce the count or handle it manually.</p><p>This feat does not automatically add proficiency with Cook's Utensils. To add it, toggle on the \"Edit\" mode of your sheet, and below your Skills click on the Cog icon to add this proficiency.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
